From: Thorch contributors
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm8550: Do not turn off USB GDSCs during gdsc_disable()

With PWRSTS_OFF_ON, USB GDSCs are turned off during gdsc_disable(). This
can happen during scenarios such as system suspend and breaks the resume
of USB controller from suspend.

So use PWRSTS_RET_ON to indicate the GDSC driver to not turn off the GDSCs
during gdsc_disable() and allow the hardware to transition the GDSCs to
retention when the parent domain enters low power state during system
suspend.

Mirrors the merged upstream SM8650 fix
clk: qcom: gcc-sm8650: Do not turn off USB GDSCs during gdsc_disable()
(SM8550 usb_1 observed faulting on resume with SID=0x40 cb=9 TF, leading
to xhci Host System Error and a dead dock until reboot).

Fixes: 955f2ea3b9e9 ("clk: qcom: Add GCC driver for SM8550")
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8550.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8550.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8550.c
@@ -3063,7 +3063,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "usb30_prim_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
 };
 
@@ -3072,7 +3072,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "usb3_phy_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
 };
 

